            },
            "kind": "ontology",
            "locator": "Term label, definition, synonym scope and chemistry annotations",
            "supports_or_contradicts": "Cysteine-HCl carries neither L nor D in its source label. MediaDive links CAS 10318-18-0 and CHEBI:52891; the latter is QSY9 succinimidyl ester rather than cysteine. The existing L-cysteine hydrochloride owner cannot supply missing stereochemistry.; JCM 680 names an L-cysteine hydrochloride monohydrate solution but gives no concentration for the 10 mL addition. The local stock identity therefore remains separate from the pure solute. CHEBI:52891 and the Thermo QSY9 product show that its QSY9 synonym is a different dye and must remain non-resolving provenance.; The source label explicitly says L-cysteine HCl, but MediaDive attaches racemic-hydrochloride CAS 10318-18-0 and QSY9 CHEBI:52891. The label suggests CHEBI:91247 but the contradictory independent fields remain unresolved.",
            "url": "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/ontologies/chebi/terms?iri=http%3A%2F%2Fpurl.obolibrary.org%2Fobo%2FCHEBI_52891",
